    "supplier's own Arabic wording; `expectedCode` is the item in the pharmacy's",
    "catalogue that the line actually refers to, established by cross-referencing",
    "the pharmacy's purchasing sheet for the same day.",
    "",
    "Only line items are kept here. Account balances, addresses, phone numbers and",
    "the pharmacy's own identifiers are deliberately left out.",
    "",
    "`expectCertain: false` marks a line that SHOULD stop and ask — either because",
    "the supplier's price has moved away from the catalogue, or because two",
    "catalogue items genuinely fit. Getting those wrong is worse than a miss."
